# Core Principles

- **Simple is best.** Choose the most direct implementation that satisfies the current requirement. No speculative abstraction: a helper, base class, or "manager" layer needs at least two real call sites to justify its existence.
- **Focus on the core loop.** This product lives or dies by one loop: AI usage → EV/EXP growth → level-up gacha → battle → CP settlement → back to usage. Prioritize work that closes or strengthens this loop. Features outside it are deferred by default (see the "deliberately not building" list in docs/product.html).
- **Don't look too far ahead.** Build for the current milestone only. Future-proofing is achieved through clean boundaries (see architecture-discipline rule), never through speculative features, unused config options, or "TODO: support X later" scaffolding.
- **No filler.** In code review, plans, and summaries: state decisions and their reasons, skip generic advice, restated requirements, and hedge words. If a section says nothing actionable, delete it.
